# Frontend Environment Variables (.env)
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.production) to configure your environment.
# Note: Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the client bundle.
# NEVER put backend secrets, database passwords, JWT secrets, or SMTP keys here.

# ==============================================================================
# Production Deployed Backend (Render / Cloud HTTPS)
# ==============================================================================
# In production Android builds, an explicit HTTPS backend URL is required.
# Replace with your confirmed Render backend URL before building the release APK:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-DEPLOYED-BACKEND.onrender.com/api

# ==============================================================================
# Local Android Development (LAN / Wi-Fi)
# ==============================================================================
# When running on physical Android devices connected to your local network.
# If omitted, the native app defaults to http://192.168.29.227:8080/api.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://<YOUR-LOCAL-IP>:8080/api

# ==============================================================================
# Local Browser Development
# ==============================================================================
# In browser dev, leave VITE_API_BASE_URL unset or set to /api to use the Vite
# development proxy configured in vite.config.ts (forwarding to localhost:8080).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
